    "created_at": "2026-03-27T12:00:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-27T12:00:07Z",
    "body": "Thanks for pointing that out. Not sure what the best option is, but given the [special treatment by the HTML parser](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#creating-and-inserting-nodes:attr-is) it IMHO it makes sense to consider the `is` attribute as code-equivalent. In spec terms, that would mean including it in \"built-in safe baseline configuration\" so that `removeUnsafe` would remove it.\n\nI wonder if the note after step 10 in [create an element for the token](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#create-an-element-for-the-token) means that is is a non-issue, though. I'd expect parses that involve the sanitizer in some way to have willExecuteScript as false.\n\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
