    "body": "> This issue was mostly fixed by [#12756](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12756), except for this point by [@otherdaniel](https://github.com/otherdaniel):\n> \n> > I do see it as a little different than regular custom elements, because you have to allow-list those individually, while `is` allows all of them in one go. Even if a particular custom element is explicitly removed in `removeElements`. It's basically the `allowCustomElements` setting in disguise, which we rejected. That said, we could certainly go either way with this.\n\nIn blink we check the `is` attribute value and apply element sanitization as if that value is the element name. I think we should do the same in the spec.",
